 17592186541881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542082 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541946 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542082 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542082 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542082 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186541487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542082 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e60fe765-3ba7-5b2e-a3cc-67f6b659f5d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542182 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542182 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143132" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542182 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542182 #edb/ref 1071 "The area of a circle decreases at a rate that's proportional to the cube of its radius. Write down a differential equation describing the rate of change of the radius, $r(t),$ in this process. Assume that $K>0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542182 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a8d62c5b-3e1c-59af-b194-160b1241f14c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542182 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **area** of a circle **decreases** at a **rate** that's **proportional** to the cube of its **radius**. *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *area $A$ of a circle* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}$ *decreases* at a rate that's *proportional* to the cube of its *radius.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=-k{r}^{3}\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0.$\n\nWe wish to use this information to find an expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe area of a circle is given by \n\n$$\nA=\\pi {r}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nDifferentiating this equation with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =2\\pi r\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-k{r}^{3} \\\\ 2\\pi r\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-k{r}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{k{r}^{3}}{2\\pi r} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{k{r}^{2}}{2\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now introduce a new constant:\n\n$$\nK=\\frac{k}{2\\pi }>0\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=-K{r}^{2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542238 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186542255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542238 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1a243f40-c3c6-58d7-bac3-52d3bb082cf4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542238 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186542182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542243 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2b8f298c-89ca-5efd-8419-026734b35b16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542243 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186542145 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542255 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186542243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542255 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "52ea8b3b-19b7-5968-bcaa-348c34bcb384" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542255 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186373862 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542256 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186542238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542256 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "53b991cc-3a22-5116-adab-cd17f3c705cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542256 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186542180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542271 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186542256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542271 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "88e7fdbd-88d3-5a0c-b233-89990b64230f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542271 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186542136 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
